# CODEOWNERS — required-review enforcement for security-critical paths.
#
# Per docs/DECISIONS/0010-payload-fixture-marker-convention.md §"Open after
# M3.1" (new-file-plus-new-marker subcase), the broad-scope marker families
# (rules-data, detector-test) defend the FILES they cover, not the
# DIRECTORY shape — so an attacker who can add a new file under a
# path-restricted directory with a fresh marker creates a scanner dead
# zone. The mitigation is governance: this CODEOWNERS file forces
# maintainer review on PRs touching those directories.
#
# Placeholder owner: @warden-sh/maintainers. The final GitHub team/handle
# is undecided pending the public-repo migration tracked in ADR 0004
# (github-org-placeholder) — see docs/ISSUES.md #002 for the open
# action item. Until the placeholder resolves, this file documents
# *intent*; GitHub will not enforce the rule until the team exists.

# Broad-scope marker families: any PR that touches the rule data or the
# marker parser itself requires maintainer review. These are the paths
# where the new-file-plus-new-marker attack class lands.
packages/rules/src/data/    @warden-sh/maintainers
packages/core/src/marker.ts @warden-sh/maintainers

# Architectural decision records are append-only and require review.
docs/DECISIONS/             @warden-sh/maintainers

# .github itself (this file + future workflows) is governance surface.
.github/                    @warden-sh/maintainers

# M5 trust root (ADR 0012 §5). The trust-layer mirror of the
# new-file-plus-new-marker class: an attacker with PR access could add
# their own SSH key to allowed_signers and then sign payloads with that
# key. Both diffs are syntactically valid; only maintainer review
# distinguishes them. The technical fix (Sigstore / threshold trust) is
# tracked in docs/ISSUES.md #006 and deferred to v1.0. Until then, this
# CODEOWNERS rule is the load-bearing defense.
.warden/trust/                  @warden-sh/maintainers
.warden/trust/allowed_signers   @warden-sh/maintainers
.warden/trust/manifest.toml     @warden-sh/maintainers
# Trust subsystem source — same governance posture as marker.ts since
# the trust pipeline determines what counts as "signed" at scan time.
packages/core/src/trust/        @warden-sh/maintainers
packages/cli/src/trust-cli.ts   @warden-sh/maintainers
